{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>The dwelling-place of the eternal Elohim.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): he says, 'Your dwelling-place is the eternal Elohim,' as in (Psalms 91:9) ״עליון שמת מעונך״, and the term מעון is like סכה (booth), and likewise (Psalms 76:3) ״ויהי בשלם סכו ומעונתו בציון״. And there is a difference between מעון (dwelling-place) and מקום (place): for the מעון is always above, over the one who shelters in it, while the מקום is below." "<b>And beneath, the arms of eternity.</b> You have the arms of eternity to support you. Or one may say: the Holy One, blessed be He, who is the eternal Elohim, is the מעון (dwelling-place) of the world — that is, He bears the upper beings; and 'beneath, the arms of eternity' means He bears the lower beings as well, for all of existence leans upon Him, as it is written (Psalms 104:2) ״נוטה שמים כיריעה״ — that is, like this curtain spread above, which hangs in the air and does not lean upon anything in the world; and it is written (Job 26:7) ״תולה ארץ על בלימה״ — that is, upon nothing, but upon His power; and a person must seal his mouth, for he cannot comprehend how this is — and the term בלימה, as it is expounded, is two words: תיבה אחת (one word); and if so, the heavens and the earth lean upon His power, may He be exalted. And likewise the prophet said (Isaiah 46:4) ״אני עשיתי ואני אשא״ — that is, I made heaven and earth, and I bear them. And He whose hand holds such great power has the power to drive the enemy from before you." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'The dwelling-place of the eternal Elohim' — the appended ה׳ alludes to the attribute of judgment, for מעון is the attribute of mercy and מעונה is the attribute of judgment. And because of this Moses mentioned here מעונה, whereas in another place he said (Psalms 90:1) ״ה׳ מעון אתה היית לנו״ — for there Moses speaks in prayer, and therefore he mentioned מעון, which alludes to the attribute of mercy; but here, where he needed to allude to the attribute of judgment in order to drive out and destroy the enemies, he mentioned מעונה with the appended ה׳, which alludes to the first ה׳ in the name 'אלהי קדם.' 'And beneath, the arms' — which are 'of eternity' (עולם); and the word זרועות is not in construct state, and the sense of the verse is thus: 'and beneath,' down to the end of the structure, which is the attribute of judgment — and this is ״ויגרש מפניך אויב״, and it is the [sefirah of] judgment. And on this account he used the expression ויאמר, which is the attribute of judgment, and this is ״ויגרש מפניך אויב״. And he did not say וחרב גאותך but rather ואשר חרב גאותך — and it is from the root of מישור (levelness/equity), that is, 'and the sword of Your majesty levels' (וישור החרב גאותך); for the sword is not the pride of Israel, heaven forbid, for it is the inheritance of Esau; rather, the intent is the attribute of judgment, since at the hour when Israel are worthy, the left becomes right. You thereby learn that Moses alluded to all ten here, just as they are alluded to in the Song of the Sea in the verse (Exodus 15:11) ״מי כמכה״ — just as he alluded to them there at the beginning of his prophecy, so now at the end of his prophecy he sealed the Torah with them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:54:37.341735878Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}